            "review_text": "mamacita1001\nSingapore, Singapore6966 contributions\n0\nA small place with a big menu\nApr 2025 • Solo\ni was back in Da Tham area after years.\n\nThere are many changes in the area as so many big bars/restaurants/clubs occupy the main streets.\n\nFortunately there are still some old and small Vietnamese restaurants on back alleys.\n\nLa Table de Saigon is one of them.\n\nWhen I saw this restaurant, I was very happy that they still have business.\nI ate here twice during my visit to Ho Chi Minh City this time.(and I did so many years ago too !) \n\nFrankly speaking, the food isn't the best but the menu range is enormous and more importantly it is very reasonable.\nIf you dine out on the main street in Da Tham, it costs more. The reason I came back here is to enjoy local food and I enjoy choosing what I want to eat from their huge  menu !!!!\n\nI always enjoy this tiny restaurant.\nTuna in claypot is awesome and very cheap. I can’t have the same with such a cheap price in my country.\nTuna Avocado wasabi salad is actually funny. Pasted wasabi tube comes with You can adjust the spiciness. DIY\n\nI enjoyed the variety of cocktails as well. \n\nThis place isn’t chic at all but I appreciate the casual style of the dining scene. I definitely come back to this restaurant next time I am in Da Tham\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten May 3, 2025",
